.\" $NetBSD$
.Dd September 4, 2026
.Dt OPENAI-C 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm openai-c
.Nd small OpenAI Responses API command-line client
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl m Ar model
.Op Fl s Ar instructions
.Op Fl Fl base-url Ar url
.Op Fl Fl ca-file Ar file
.Op Fl Fl raw
.Op Ar prompt ...
.Nm
.Fl Fl extract
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends a text prompt to the OpenAI Responses API over a verified TLS
connection and prints the returned output text.
If no prompt arguments are present, the prompt is read from standard input.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl m Ar model , Fl Fl model Ar model
Select the model.  The default is
.Dq gpt-5-mini .
.It Fl s Ar text , Fl Fl instructions Ar text
Send developer instructions with the prompt.
.It Fl Fl base-url Ar url
Use an alternate HTTPS API base URL.
.It Fl Fl ca-file Ar file
Use the named PEM CA bundle for certificate verification.
.It Fl Fl raw
Print the complete JSON response instead of extracting output text.
.It Fl Fl extract
Read a saved Responses API JSON document from standard input and print its
output text without making a network request.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Print the program version.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Print a short usage message.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width OPENAI_ORGANIZATION
.It Ev OPENAI_API_KEY
Required API key.
.It Ev OPENAI_MODEL
Model used when no command-line model is given.
.It Ev OPENAI_BASE_URL
HTTPS API base URL; defaults to
.Pa https://api.openai.com/v1 .
.It Ev OPENAI_ORGANIZATION
Optional organization identifier header.
.It Ev OPENAI_PROJECT
Optional project identifier header.
.It Ev SSL_CERT_FILE
PEM CA bundle used instead of the pkgsrc Mozilla root certificate bundle.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
openai-c "Explain OpenVMS logical names briefly"
printf '%s\n' "Summarize this input" | openai-c -m gpt-5-mini
openai-c --extract < saved-response.json
.Ed
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Configuration and usage errors return 1, network or TLS errors return 2,
HTTP API errors return 3, and malformed or text-free JSON responses return 4.
